at defends against infection and cancer.":"691f28b4204c","The chapter combines several approaches by emphasizing abnormal behavior that is distressing and harmful to the self or others.":"f92923c302e9","The chapter contrasts antisocial personality disorder (low remorse/empathy and disregard for rules), borderline personality disorder (unstable relationships, self-image, and emotion), and narcissistic personality disorder (grandiosity, need for admiration, low empathy).":"ff755637d4dc","The chapter describes anxiety as involving strong negative emotions and physical tension arising from anticipation of danger.":"b17b163e1a77","The chapter describes severe early-life stress as being associated with heightened amygdala responses, norepinephrine-system hyperactivity, increased HPA responses, reduced hippocampal neurogenesis, and greater later vulnerability to stress.":"20f5daf19d88","The chapter emphasizes that the heart-disease risk associated with Type A personality is driven especially by hostility rather than competitiveness alone.":"539f7c00a3fc","The chapter identifies hope, resilience, spirituality, and gratitude as traits that contribute to well-being.":"750d5375b601","The chapter identifies smoking as the leading preventable cause of death in the United States and highlights exercise, healthy weight, and a balanced diet as important health behaviors.":"60b7a0695c13","The chapter identifies the anterior cingulate as an important brain structure in the regulation of emotion.":"cdad2634c82c","The chapter notes disparities in access to mental-health care and states that poverty is an important risk factor for psychological disorders.":"05657607d8ab","The chapter quiz identifies enlarged brain ventricles as a biological finding reliably associated with schizophrenia.":"e7a0286025a8","The chapter quiz states that once basic needs are met, additional money does not guarantee greater happiness.":"898300671e92","The chapter quiz uses the World Health Organization defini